</script>

# Collapsible

Shows and hides one section of content, such as extra rows or advanced settings. The trigger sets `aria-expanded` and `aria-controls`, and the content slides open and closed. Use `Accordion` instead for a list of sections that work together.

<Demo />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Collapsible, CollapsibleTrigger, CollapsibleContent } from "#lib/components/ui/collapsible/index.js";
	import { ChevronsUpDownIcon } from "@lucide/svelte";
</script>

<Collapsible>
	<header>
		<h4>@peduarte starred 3 repositories</h4>
		<CollapsibleTrigger variant="ghost" size="icon-sm" aria-label="Toggle repositories">
			<ChevronsUpDownIcon />
		</CollapsibleTrigger>
	</header>
	<div>@radix-ui/primitives</div>
	<CollapsibleContent>
		<div>@radix-ui/colors</div>
		<div>@stitches/react</div>
	</CollapsibleContent>
</Collapsible>
```

## Installation

```pm
npx remote0 add https://plainsv.com/r/collapsible.json
```

## Anatomy

`Collapsible` holds the open state and renders an unstyled `div`, so lay out its parts with a `class`. `CollapsibleTrigger` toggles the content, and `CollapsibleContent` renders its children only while open. Content outside `CollapsibleContent` always shows.

## Trigger

`CollapsibleTrigger` renders an outline `Button` and passes `variant`, `size`, `rounded`, and other button attributes to it. To toggle from any other element, pass a `trigger` snippet. It receives `props` with the ids, `aria-expanded`, `data-state`, `disabled`, and an `onclick` that toggles the content. Spread them onto the element.

<Demo section="trigger" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<CollapsibleTrigger>
	{#snippet trigger({ props })}
		<button type="button" {...props}>
			<ChevronRightIcon />
			Advanced settings
		</button>
	{/snippet}
</CollapsibleTrigger>
```

Every part sets `data-state` to `open` or `closed`, so you can style the trigger by its state, such as turning a chevron while open.

## Controlled

Use `bind:open` to open or close the content from your own code, or `onOpenChange` to run code on each toggle. Without either, set `defaultOpen` to start open.

<Demo section="controlled" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<script lang="ts">
	import { Collapsible, CollapsibleTrigger, CollapsibleContent } from "#lib/components/ui/collapsible/index.js";

	let isOpen = $state(false);
</script>

<Collapsible bind:open={isOpen}>
	<CollapsibleTrigger>{isOpen ? "Hide" : "Show"} details</CollapsibleTrigger>
	<CollapsibleContent>
		<p>The details are open.</p>
	</CollapsibleContent>
</Collapsible>
```

A passed `onclick` on the default trigger runs before the toggle. Call `e.preventDefault()` in it to keep the current state.

## States

Set `disabled` on `Collapsible` to disable the trigger and keep the content in its current state. The root sets `data-disabled` for custom styles.

<Demo section="states" />

```svelte title="+page.svelte"
<Collapsible defaultOpen disabled>
	<CollapsibleTrigger>Disabled</CollapsibleTrigger>
	<CollapsibleContent>
		<p>The trigger is disabled, so this stays open.</p>
	</CollapsibleContent>
</Collapsible>
```

## API

`Collapsible` and `CollapsibleContent` extend the native `div` attributes. `CollapsibleTrigger` passes extra attributes to its `Button`, and ignores them when a `trigger` snippet is given.

```ts title="index.ts"
interface Props extends CompPropsWithChild<"div"> {
	/** Whether the content is shown; supports `bind:open` */
	open?: boolean;
	/** Starting state when `open` is not set; defaults to `false` */
	defaultOpen?: boolean;
	/** Called when the content opens or closes */
	onOpenChange?: (open: boolean) => void;
	/** Blocks opening and closing */
	disabled?: boolean;
}

interface TriggerProps extends Omit<CompProps<"button">, "children"> {
	/** Label for the default trigger button */
	children?: Snippet;
	/** Custom trigger; spread `props` onto the element that toggles the content */
	trigger?: Snippet<[{ props: TriggerAttrs }]>;
	/** Visual style of the default button; defaults to `outline` */
	variant?: ButtonProps["variant"];
	/** Size of the default button, including the square `icon-*` sizes; defaults to `md` */
	size?: ButtonProps["size"];
	/** Corner radius of the default button; follows `size` when omitted */
	rounded?: UiRounded;
}
```
